<Layout title="Privacy Policy — License Expiration Tracker (Chrome)" description="Privacy policy for the License Expiration Tracker Chrome extension by Cornerstone Licensing. License entries are stored locally; we do not sell personal information.">
  <section class="page-hero">
    <div class="container">
      <h1>Privacy Policy — License Expiration Tracker (Chrome)</h1>
      <p>Last updated: September 7, 2026</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container article" style="max-width: 720px;">
      <h2>About This Policy</h2>
      <p>This privacy policy describes how the <strong>License Expiration Tracker</strong> Chrome extension (“the Extension”) handles information. The Extension is a product of Cornerstone Licensing, published by <strong>Cornerstone Support LLC d/b/a Cornerstone Licensing</strong> (“Cornerstone,” “we,” “us,” or “our”).</p>
      <p>The Extension helps you track business license and expiration dates. It is a local-first tool: entries you add are stored in Chrome storage on your device. It is not an advertising product, and we do not sell personal information.</p>

      <h2>Summary</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>The Extension tracks license and expiration dates that you enter.</li>
        <li>Those entries, your settings, and local notification state are stored locally in Chrome storage.</li>
        <li>We do not sell personal information.</li>
        <li>The Extension is not used for advertising and does not show ads.</li>
        <li>Your license inventory is not sent to Cornerstone for ads or analytics.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>What the Extension Handles</h2>
      <p>The Extension handles only information needed for its single purpose—helping you keep track of licenses and their expiration dates:</p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>License details you enter</strong>, such as license name, type, jurisdiction, license or certificate number, expiration date, notes, and similar fields you choose to save.</li>
        <li><strong>Settings</strong> you configure in the Extension (for example, reminder preferences and display options).</li>
        <li><strong>Local notification state</strong> used to schedule, show, or dismiss reminders on this device.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>The Extension does not require an account. You decide what to enter. Do not store information in the Extension that you do not want kept on this browser profile.</p>

      <h2>How Information Is Used</h2>
      <p>Information handled by the Extension is used only to:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Display your license items and expiration dates in the Extension interface.</li>
        <li>Provide local reminders so you can act before a license expires.</li>
        <li>Maintain your settings across sessions on this browser profile.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>We do not use Extension data to build advertising profiles, to sell or rent lists, or to market unrelated products inside the Extension.</p>

      <h2>Storage and Transmission</h2>
      <p>License entries, settings, and notification state are stored locally using Chrome storage associated with your browser profile. They remain on your device (or in your Chrome profile sync, if you have Chrome sync enabled for extension data).</p>
      <p>The Extension does not send your license inventory to Cornerstone for advertising or analytics. We do not operate a remote database of your Extension entries as part of the current product.</p>
      <p>If Chrome sync is enabled, Google may sync extension storage as part of your Chrome profile under Google’s own terms and privacy policy. That sync is controlled by your Google account and Chrome settings, not by a Cornerstone server.</p>
      <p>If we later add optional cloud features (for example, signed-in backup or multi-device sync operated by Cornerstone), we will update this policy before those features collect or transmit license inventory to our systems, and we will describe what is sent and why.</p>

      <h2>Permissions</h2>
      <p>The Extension requests only the Chrome permissions needed for its single purpose: storing and displaying the license items you enter, maintaining settings, and providing local reminders. It does not request permissions to read your general browsing history, inject ads, or collect data unrelated to license tracking.</p>

      <h2>Sharing</h2>
      <p>We do not sell, rent, or trade personal information. We do not share your license inventory with third parties for advertising or analytics.</p>
      <p>We may disclose information if required by law, legal process, or to protect the rights, safety, or property of Cornerstone, our users, or others—only to the extent we actually possess that information. Because the current Extension is local-first, Cornerstone typically does not hold your license inventory on our servers.</p>
      <p>This website (licensingmadesimple.com) and other Cornerstone services have their own practices. Using those services is separate from using the Extension. See the <a href="/privacy">LicensingMadeSimple privacy policy</a> for this website.</p>

      <h2>Retention</h2>
      <p>Information stored by the Extension remains in Chrome storage until you delete an item, clear the Extension’s data, uninstall the Extension, or otherwise remove it from this browser profile. We do not operate a remote retention period for local Extension entries because we do not receive that inventory today.</p>
      <p>If you contact us by email, phone, or mail, we retain the correspondence you send for as long as needed to respond and to meet ordinary business and legal records needs, then delete or archive it according to our internal practices.</p>

      <h2>Children’s Privacy</h2>
      <p>The Extension is intended for business licensing use by adults. It is not directed to children under 13, and we do not knowingly collect personal information from children under 13. If you believe a child has provided information through the Extension or by contacting us, please use the contact details below and we will take appropriate steps to delete it.</p>

      <h2>Your Choices</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>You control what license details you enter and can edit or delete items in the Extension at any time.</li>
        <li>You can change or disable reminder settings in the Extension.</li>
        <li>You can remove stored Extension data by clearing the Extension’s storage or uninstalling the Extension from Chrome.</li>
        <li>Chrome notification and sync settings are controlled in your browser and Google account.</li>
        <li>To ask a question about this policy, or to request access to, correction of, or deletion of personal information you have sent us directly (for example, by email), contact us using the details below.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Changes to This Policy</h2>
      <p>We may update this privacy policy from time to time. The “Last updated” date at the top of this page will change when we do. Material changes—especially any change that would involve transmitting license inventory to Cornerstone or a third party—will be posted on this page before those practices begin. Continued use of the Extension after an update means you accept the revised policy.</p>

      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p>Questions about this policy or the License Expiration Tracker Chrome extension:</p>
      <p>
        Cornerstone Support LLC d/b/a Cornerstone Licensing<br />
        925 North Point Parkway, Suite 470<br />
        Alpharetta, GA 30005<br />
        Email: <a href="mailto:jeff@cornerstonelicensing.com">jeff@cornerstonelicensing.com</a><br />
        Phone: <a href="tel:+17705874595">770-587-4595</a>
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>

